// EXPECT_COMPILE_ERROR E_COERCE_GENERIC_PATTERN_UNSUPPORTED
//
// Plan 214.1 (D429 amend, §generic-образцы) fix: a receiver generic ARG that
// is itself a NESTED/structured shape (`OneBox[Vec[T]]`, not a bare carrier
// type-param `OneBox[T]`) must be rejected — the shallow one-directional
// unifier (`unify_coerce_receiver`, R4 "без рекурсии вглубь") only binds
// bare top-level slots, it cannot bind INTO `Vec[T]`'s own nested `T`.
//
// This shape actually PARSES (the original `collect_coerce_pairs` comment
// claiming `Type[Vec[T]]` is a parse error was wrong — carrier-position
// nested types are legal grammar since Plan 153.5/D263, for the
// monomorphizer's `[]T`/`Vec[Vec[T]]` receiver-binding use case); it is the
// GATE that must actually observe and reject it, not the grammar.
//
// Doubly dangerous if silently accepted: the receiver's structural form
// (`Vec[T]`) is not itself enforced anywhere (pre-existing gap, registry
// #88) — an accepted-but-unvalidated pattern here would apply to ANY
// `OneBox` instance, not just ones actually wrapping a `Vec`.
module neg.d429_1_generic_coerce_structured_receiver_neg

type OneBox[T] value { ro v T }

#coerce
export fn OneBox[Vec[T]] @first() -> ro T => @v[0]

fn main() {
    println("unreached")
}
